msgid "2.1. PostgreSQL"
msgstr "2.1. PostgreSQL"

#: ../../admin/launch_setup/launcher_server/migration_from_compose.rst:290
msgid "Параметры ``pg_dump``:"
msgstr "``pg_dump`` parameters:"

#: ../../admin/launch_setup/launcher_server/migration_from_compose.rst:292
msgid ""
"``-F c`` -- формат custom (компактный, поддерживает параллельный restore)."
msgstr "``-F c`` — custom format (compact, supports parallel restore)."

#: ../../admin/launch_setup/launcher_server/migration_from_compose.rst:293
msgid ""
"``--no-owner --no-acl`` -- выкидываем ``OWNER TO`` / ``GRANT`` (на target "
"пользователи называются иначе, ownership проставит ``pg_restore --role``)."
msgstr ""
"``--no-owner --no-acl`` — strips ``OWNER TO`` / ``GRANT`` statements (target"
" users have different names; ownership will be set by ``pg_restore "
"--role``)."

#: ../../admin/launch_setup/launcher_server/migration_from_compose.rst:294
msgid ""
"``--clean --if-exists`` НЕ используем -- целевую БД чистим отдельно командой"
" ``DROP SCHEMA``."
msgstr ""
"``--clean --if-exists`` is NOT used — the target database is cleaned "
"separately with a ``DROP SCHEMA`` command."

#: ../../admin/launch_setup/launcher_server/migration_from_compose.rst:295
msgid ""
"Без ``-f /tmp/...`` -- ``pg_dump`` пишет в stdout, мы перенаправляем ``>`` в"
" файл на хосте."
msgstr ""
"Without ``-f /tmp/...`` — ``pg_dump`` writes to stdout, which we redirect "
"``>`` to a file on the host."

#: ../../admin/launch_setup/launcher_server/migration_from_compose.rst:299
msgid ""
"**Если какая-то из БД отсутствует на вашем source** (например, в community-"
"only deployment нет ``ecos_edi``) -- ``pg_dump`` упадёт с ``database "
"\"<name>\" does not exist``. Просто пропустите соответствующий блок: "
"соответствующая target-БД на launcher2 либо отсутствует, либо останется "
"пустой и Liquibase webapp'а наполнит её при первом старте."
msgstr ""
"**If any of the databases is missing on your source** (for example, "
"``ecos_edi`` does not exist in a community-only deployment) — ``pg_dump`` "
"will fail with ``database \"<name>\" does not exist``. Simply skip the "
"corresponding block: the corresponding target database on launcher2 either "
"does not exist or will remain empty and be populated by the webapp's "
"Liquibase on first startup."

